{"name":"Field Time Green","hex":"#649050","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"field","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A land area free of woodland, cities, and towns; an area of open country.","The open country near or belonging to a town or city."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To intercept or catch (a ball) and play it.","To be the team catching and throwing the ball, as opposed to hitting it."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/field"},{"term":"time","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The inevitable progression into the future with the passing of present and past events.","The feeling of the passage of events and their relative duration, as experienced by an individual."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To measure or record the time, duration, or rate of something.","To choose when something commences or its duration."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/time"},{"term":"green","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of grass and leaves; a primary additive color midway between yellow and blue which is evoked by light between roughly 495–570 nm.","A member of a green party; an environmentalist."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a green hue.","Sickly, unwell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/green"}],"entries":[{"title":"Time","blocks":[{"text":"Time is the continuous progression of existence that occurs in an apparently irreversible succession from the past, through the present, and into the future. Time dictates all forms of action, age, and causality, being a component quantity of various measurements used to sequence events, to compare the duration of events or the intervals between them, and to quantify rates of change of quantities in material reality or in conscious experience. Time is often referred to as the fourth dimension and the temporal dimension, in addition to the three spatial dimensions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/MontreGousset001.jpg/330px-MontreGousset001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Time","wikidata":"Q11471"},{"title":"Green","blocks":[{"text":"Green is the color between cyan and yellow on the visible spectrum. It has 295–350 different shades. It is evoked by light which has a dominant wavelength of roughly 495–570 nm. In subtractive color systems, used in painting and color printing, it is created by a combination of yellow and cyan; in the RGB color model, used on television and computer screens, it is one of the additive primary colors, along with red and blue, which are mixed in different combinations to create all other colors. By far the largest contributor to green in nature is chlorophyll, the chemical by which plants photosynthesize and convert sunlight into chemical energy. Many creatures have adapted to their green environments by taking on a green hue themselves as camouflage. Several minerals have a green color, including the emerald, which is colored green by its chromium content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg/330px-Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green","wikidata":"Q3133"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Wooden_hourglass_3.jpg/500px-Wooden_hourglass_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Wooden_hourglass_3.jpg/500px-Wooden_hourglass_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The flow of sand in an hourglass can be used to measure the passage of one hour of time. It also concretely represents the present as being between the past and the future.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWooden_hourglass_3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Canberra_%28AU%29%2C_Albert_Hall%2C_Sundial_--_2019_--_1740.jpg/500px-Canberra_%28AU%29%2C_Albert_Hall%2C_Sundial_--_2019_--_1740.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Canberra_%28AU%29%2C_Albert_Hall%2C_Sundial_--_2019_--_1740.jpg/1280px-Canberra_%28AU%29%2C_Albert_Hall%2C_Sundial_--_2019_--_1740.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Canberra_%28AU%29%2C_Albert_Hall%2C_Sundial_--_2019_--_1740.jpg/500px-Canberra_%28AU%29%2C_Albert_Hall%2C_Sundial_--_2019_--_1740.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Horizontal sundial in Canberra","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACanberra_(AU)%2C_Albert_Hall%2C_Sundial_--_2019_--_1740.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Florence-Duomo-Clock.jpg/330px-Florence-Duomo-Clock.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Florence-Duomo-Clock.jpg/330px-Florence-Duomo-Clock.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"24-hour clock face in Florence","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlorence-Duomo-Clock.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Swatch_Irony_angle_below.jpg/500px-Swatch_Irony_angle_below.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Swatch_Irony_angle_below.jpg/1280px-Swatch_Irony_angle_below.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/